---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProductFlow from '../components/ProductFlow.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const useCases = [
  { title: 'Owner operations', body: 'Turn a broad operating question into a short, reviewable decision queue.', href: '/use-cases/owner-operations/' },
  { title: 'AI receptionist', body: 'Give inbound conversations a clear path to a person, a next step, or an approved workflow.', href: '/use-cases/ai-receptionist/' },
  { title: 'Speed to lead', body: 'Bring new opportunities into view while the context is still useful.', href: '/use-cases/speed-to-lead/' },
  { title: 'No-show rescheduling', body: 'Coordinate the follow-up work around a missed appointment without hiding the decision.', href: '/use-cases/no-show-rescheduling/' },
  { title: 'Sales to operations', body: 'Carry the important context from a won job into the team responsible for delivery.', href: '/use-cases/sales-to-operations/' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is Rokko?', a: 'Rokko is an AI operations teammate being built for home-service companies. It is designed to help teams inspect live operating context, prepare the next supported move, and keep consequential actions under human authority.' },
  { q: 'Does Rokko make changes without approval?', a: 'The public product direction is approval-bounded: consequential actions should be presented for review before execution. The exact approval policy is configured around the workflow and must be verified during implementation.' },
  { q: 'Is Rokko a chatbot?', a: 'No. Conversation is an interface, not the whole product. The operating model connects questions, workflow context, approvals, and clear outcomes.' },
  { q: 'Which systems does Rokko integrate with?', a: 'The integration surface is being verified. Rokko does not publish a marketplace or promise specific connectors before they are approved for the launch scope.' },
  { q: 'How is pricing structured?', a: 'Public pricing has not been approved. Rokko will not publish invented plan names, fees, limits, or contract terms.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero__grid">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">AI operations teammate for home services</p>
        <h1>Ask the business.<br /><span class="display-accent">Approve the next move.</span></h1>
        <p class="deck">
          Rokko is the AI operations teammate for home-service companies. From Slack, it checks live CRM context, coordinates appointments and pipeline work, and waits for approval before it changes anything.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button button--primary" href={site.demoPath}>Book a tailored demo</a>
          <a class="button button--secondary" href="#core-flow">See Rokko in action</a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero__note">Product direction shown with an illustrative, customer-safe workflow.</p>
      </div>
      <ProductFlow />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="boundary" aria-label="Rokko product boundary">
    <div class="container boundary__grid">
      <span>Live operating context</span>
      <span>Visible owner approval</span>
      <span>Clear outcome states</span>
      <span>Home-service focus</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper problem">
    <div class="container--content grid-2 problem__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The operating problem</p>
        <h2>Your business already knows what happened. The hard part is deciding <span class="display-accent">what happens next.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="problem__copy">
        <p class="deck">The signal is spread across appointments, conversations, pipeline stages, notes, and people. Getting a trustworthy answer often means opening five tabs, asking three people, and still wondering whether the record is current.</p>
        <div class="rule"></div>
        <dl class="signal-list">
          <div><dt>01</dt><dd>Questions lose time while context is assembled.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>02</dt><dd>Actions drift when ownership is not explicit.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>03</dt><dd>Automation creates risk when authority disappears.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="core-flow" class="section section--moss flow-section">
    <div class="container--content">
      <div class="flow-section__intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">The operating model</p>
        <h2>Ask → Approve → <span class="display-accent">Verified</span></h2>
        <p class="deck">A conversational entry point, an explicit decision boundary, and a result the team can inspect.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-grid">
        <article>
          <span>01 / Ask</span>
          <h3>Start with the operating question.</h3>
          <p>Rokko is designed to assemble the relevant context around the question instead of making the operator hunt through systems.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02 / Approve</span>
          <h3>Keep authority with the team.</h3>
          <p>When a move matters, the proposed action and its basis remain visible before anything consequential proceeds.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03 / Verified</span>
          <h3>Return the outcome, not just a reply.</h3>
          <p>The result comes back with a clear state, the supporting context, and what still needs attention.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section layers">
    <div class="container--content">
      <div class="layers__heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Three coordinated layers</p>
          <h2>One teammate across the operating day.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="deck">The direction is broader than a chat window and more controlled than unattended automation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="numbered-card">
          <span class="numbered-card__number">Layer 01</span>
          <h3>Owner operations</h3>
          <p>Questions, priorities, and decision queues that help an owner see where attention is needed.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="numbered-card">
          <span class="numbered-card__number">Layer 02</span>
          <h3>Customer conversations</h3>
          <p>Inbound communication with a defined path to human review and supported operating workflows.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="numbered-card">
          <span class="numbered-card__number">Layer 03</span>
          <h3>Workflow coordination</h3>
          <p>Appointments, pipeline work, and handoffs brought into a consistent approval model.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper trace">
    <div class="container--content">
      <div class="grid-2 trace__top">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">End-to-end clarity</p>
          <h2>Every move should have a visible state.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="deck">A simple event trace makes the operating boundary legible to the person responsible for the outcome.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="event-trace">
        <li><span>08:42</span><strong>Question received</strong><small>Scope identified</small></li>
        <li><span>08:43</span><strong>Context assembled</strong><small>Source recorded</small></li>
        <li><span>08:44</span><strong>Approval requested</strong><small>Authority visible</small></li>
        <li><span>08:47</span><strong>Outcome returned</strong><small>Status explicit</small></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section use-cases">
    <div class="container--content">
      <div class="use-cases__heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Use cases</p>
          <h2>Start where operating friction is already expensive.</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/use-cases/">Explore all use cases</a>
      </div>
      <div class="use-case-list">
        {useCases.map((item, index) => (
          <a href={item.href}>
            <span>0{index + 1}</span>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.body}</p>
            <strong aria-hidden="true">↗</strong>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark implementation">
    <div class="container--content">
      <div class="grid-2 implementation__intro">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Implementation</p>
          <h2>Begin with one operating question worth answering well.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="deck">The rollout model is designed to create a reviewable boundary before expanding the workflow surface.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="implementation__steps">
        <li><span>01</span><strong>Map</strong><p>Choose the question, context, owner, and safe operating boundary.</p></li>
        <li><span>02</span><strong>Configure</strong><p>Define the source, proposed action, and required approval state.</p></li>
        <li><span>03</span><strong>Pilot</strong><p>Run the workflow with an explicit proof standard and human review.</p></li>
        <li><span>04</span><strong>Operate</strong><p>Expand only after the outcomes and authority model are understood.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section proof">
    <div class="container--content grid-2 proof__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The proof standard</p>
        <h2>No invented metrics. No mystery actions.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="deck">Rokko is not publishing customer logos, outcome claims, plan limits, or case-study numbers until they have an approved source.</p>
        <p>Proof will be tied to a defined workflow, a visible starting point, and an outcome that the operator can verify. That is slower than filling a page with generic claims. It is also more useful.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper security">
    <div class="container--content security__grid">
      <div class="security__mark" aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="/brand/gorokko-symbol-color.svg" alt="" width="160" height="160" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Trust by operating design</p>
        <h2>Authority should remain visible at the moment it matters.</h2>
        <p class="deck">Rokko’s public security and deployment specifics are still under review. The approved direction begins with least-necessary context, explicit approval for consequential moves, and inspectable outcomes.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/security/">Read the security posture</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section faq">
    <div class="container--content faq__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Frequently asked</p>
        <h2>Clear answers, including where the answer is not public yet.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        {faqs.map((item) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{item.q}</summary>
            <p>{item.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--moss final-cta">
    <div class="container--content final-cta__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The next operating question</p>
        <h2>Bring the workflow.<br /><span class="display-accent">Keep the authority.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="deck">A tailored demo starts with the part of your operation that already demands too many tabs, handoffs, and follow-ups.</p>
        <a class="button button--primary" href={site.demoPath}>Book a tailored demo</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8.5rem);
  }

  .hero__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .hero .deck {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .hero__note {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    color: var(--grk-text-muted);
    font-family: var(--grk-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .boundary {
    border-block: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
  }

  .boundary__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .boundary__grid span {
    display: flex;
    min-height: 5rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
    font-family: var(--grk-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .boundary__grid span:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; }
  .boundary__grid span:nth-last-child(-n + 2) { border-bottom: 0; }

  .problem__grid {
    align-items: start;
  }

  .problem h2 {
    max-width: 13ch;
  }

  .problem__copy {
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .signal-list {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .signal-list div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr;
    padding-block: 1.1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
  }

  .signal-list dt {
    color: var(--grk-cobalt);
    font-family: var(--grk-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  .signal-list dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .flow-section__intro {
    display: grid;
    max-width: 54rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 7rem);
  }

  .flow-section__intro h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .flow-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    background: rgb(252 251 247 / 0.18);
    border: 1px solid rgb(252 251 247 / 0.18);
  }

  .flow-grid article {
    min-height: 21rem;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.75rem);
    background: var(--grk-moss);
  }

  .flow-grid article > span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: clamp(4rem, 7vw, 7rem);
    color: var(--grk-success);
    font-family: var(--grk-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .flow-grid h3 {
    max-width: 16ch;
  }

  .flow-grid p {
    color: rgb(252 251 247 / 0.66);
  }

  .layers__heading,
  .use-cases__heading {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
  }

  .layers__heading h2,
  .use-cases__heading h2 {
    max-width: 13ch;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .trace__top {
    align-items: end;
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
  }

  .trace h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
  }

  .event-trace {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .event-trace li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 4rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding-block: 1.35rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
  }

  .event-trace span,
  .event-trace small {
    color: var(--grk-text-muted);
    font-family: var(--grk-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .event-trace small {
    grid-column: 2;
  }

  .use-cases__heading {
    align-items: end;
  }

  .use-case-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
  }

  .use-case-list a {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr auto;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
    min-height: 8rem;
    padding-block: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: padding var(--grk-duration-control) var(--grk-ease-standard), background var(--grk-duration-control) var(--grk-ease-standard);
  }

  .use-case-list a:hover {
    padding-inline: 1rem;
    background: var(--grk-paper);
  }

  .use-case-list span {
    color: var(--grk-cobalt);
    font-family: var(--grk-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  .use-case-list h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .use-case-list p {
    grid-column: 2 / -1;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--grk-text-muted);
  }

  .implementation__intro {
    align-items: end;
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem);
  }

  .implementation h2 {
    max-width: 13ch;
  }

  .implementation__steps {
    display: grid;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(252 251 247 / 0.2);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .implementation__steps li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr;
    padding-block: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(252 251 247 / 0.2);
  }

  .implementation__steps span {
    color: var(--grk-success);
    font-family: var(--grk-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  .implementation__steps strong {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .implementation__steps p {
    grid-column: 2;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    color: rgb(252 251 247 / 0.65);
  }

  .proof__grid {
    align-items: start;
  }

  .proof h2 {
    max-width: 10ch;
  }

  .security__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .security__mark {
    display: grid;
    min-height: 22rem;
    place-items: center;
    background: var(--grk-limestone);
    border: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
  }

  .security__mark img {
    width: clamp(7rem, 16vw, 11rem);
  }

  .security h2 {
    max-width: 13ch;
  }

  .faq__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 7rem);
  }

  .faq h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
  }

  .faq details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
  }

  .faq details:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grk-border);
  }

  .faq summary {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    min-height: 4.75rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1rem 2.5rem 1rem 0;
    font-weight: 650;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }

  .faq summary::after {
    position: absolute;
    right: 0;
    content: '+';
    color: var(--grk-cobalt);
    font-family: var(--grk-font-mono);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .faq details[open] summary::after { content: '−'; }
  .faq details p { color: var(--grk-text-muted); }

  .final-cta__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 7rem);
    align-items: end;
  }

  .final-cta h2 {
    max-width: 13ch;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .final-cta .deck {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .boundary__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    }

    .boundary__grid span {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .boundary__grid span:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 1px solid var(--grk-border); }
    .boundary__grid span:last-child { border-right: 0; }

    .flow-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }

    .layers__heading,
    .use-cases__heading {
      grid-template-columns: 1.35fr 0.65fr;
    }

    .event-trace li {
      grid-template-columns: 5rem 1fr auto;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .event-trace small { grid-column: auto; }

    .use-case-list a {
      grid-template-columns: 4rem 0.9fr 1.2fr auto;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .use-case-list p { grid-column: auto; }

    .implementation__steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }

    .implementation__steps li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      min-height: 17rem;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border-right: 1px solid rgb(252 251 247 / 0.2);
    }

    .implementation__steps li:last-child { border-right: 0; }
    .implementation__steps strong { margin-top: 4rem; }
    .implementation__steps p { grid-column: 1; }

    .security__grid { grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.15fr; }
    .faq__grid { grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr; }
    .final-cta__grid { grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr; }
  }

  @media (min-width: 68rem) {
    .hero__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.08fr) minmax(28rem, 0.92fr);
    }
  }
</style>
